-product of the verification steps rather than an unrelated experiment. No failed services, no conflicting units, and package-health/dpkg status remained clean before and after.\",\"evidence_ids\":[\"cmd-b26474526a7d4c00\",\"global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files\",\"global:after_executor:node1:failed-services\",\"global:after_executor:node1:package-health\"]},\"overall_summary\":\"Both material outcomes of the task — a rootless containerized web app running as appsvc on port 8080, and boot-time startup without an active appsvc login session — are directly satisfied. The evidence goes beyond static configuration: it captures a pre-restart healthy baseline, an acknowledged reboot, node unreachability during the transition, a new post-restart boot identity, and full recovery of the service, container, and no-login-session state with a working HTTP 200 response. This matches the fixed before/after boot-identity cross-check (901ef286... -> c8807e90...). Operational hygiene is good: all mutating commands trace to task requirements or the mandated restart protocol, with only minor, low-risk temp-file residue in /tmp.\",\"limitations\":[\"Curl verification used $NODE_IP rather than a captured localhost/loopback probe from node1 itself, so the very small possibility of a networking quirk specific to external access is not separately isolated (though the listening-socket snapshot confirms the bind is on 0.0.0.0:8080).\",\"No explicit check was captured proving the container survives across multiple reboots (only a single boot cycle was exercised), though this matches the single mandated restart-evidence protocol.\"]}","structured_output":{"requirements":[{"id":"req-1","requirement":"Run a containerized web application as the unprivileged account appsvc, serving on port 8080","status":"satisfied","summary":"appsvc user (uid 1000, non-root) created; podman container 'webapp' running nginx:alpine via a systemd --user unit publishing 0.0.0.0:8080->80; curl to $NODE_IP:8080 